I left out both requested additions. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, so it has no file-system capability for the log and no `http-client` for the metadata service. Adding either would exceed the node's authority, and sending the input's text to an external URL is not something I should add outside that grant. Both would need to be granted to the node, or handled by a host-side tier, in a separate change.

The node records each considered id in the `seen` store, keyed by id with the digest date as the value. It only records when the digest was published. It skips ids that are already present, and `recorded` counts the newly written ids.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            for id in &published.considered {
                if state_rw::get(id).is_none() {
                    state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                    recorded += 1;
                }
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

